<title>GREECE: Greek Alpha Leasing to up 96 dividend.</title>
<headline>Greek Alpha Leasing to up 96 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpha Credit Bank subsidiary Alpha Leasing said its fiscal 1996 pretax profit rose 7.9 percent to 7.097 billion drachmas from 6.574 billion a year earlier.</p>
<p>The company's board will propose to the annual shareholders meeting a dividend per share of 650 drachmas versus 600 drachmas in 1995.  </p>
<p>The company said its total assets rose 5.3 percent to 45.31 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>Shares of Alpha Leasing jumped 495 drachmas, 8.0 percent, in early trade to 6,690.</p>
</text>
